Example: leave a rising market completely, then buy back in later.
The FUND quote rises by 10 USD on the first of every month, from 100 USD in
January to 210 USD in December. Only Assets:Fund is selected for the report.
Salary funds one unit bought for 100 USD on 2023-01-01. It is sold for 130 USD
on 2023-04-01, leaving zero FUND units through July despite rising quotes.
The 130 USD proceeds remain in Assets:Cash. An additional 40 USD bonus funds
the 170 USD repurchase on 2023-08-01. One unit is still held on 2023-12-31,
valued at the latest quote of 210 USD from December 1.
The selected fund has flows of +100, -130, and +170 USD, so net contributions
are 140 USD. Ending value 210 minus opening value 0 minus contributions 140
gives 70 USD profit. The time-weighted factors are 130 / 100 before the sale
and 210 / 170 after the repurchase; gains while holding zero units do not
enter the return. Their product minus one is 60.59%.
Annualizing that return over January 1 to December 31 (364 days), including
the months without selected holdings, gives 60.80%.
The investor cash flows are -100 USD on January 1, +130 on April 1, -170 on
August 1, and +210 on December 31. The annual rate r solves
-100 + 130 / (1 + r)^(90 / 365) - 170 / (1 + r)^(212 / 365)
  + 210 / (1 + r)^(364 / 365) = 0, giving 103.45% annualized.
Compounding that rate over the 364-day interval gives 103.05% total.

========== CLI ==========

ledlight investment-performance --accounts Assets:Fund --include-commodities FUND --from 2023-01-01 --to 2023-12-31 --format text

